# The cross-language contract goldens are checked for content equality by
# `npm run contract:check`, and git's CRLF checkout on Windows
# (core.autocrlf=true) would otherwise make every golden look stale on a
# pristine clone. Pinning them to LF keeps the on-disk form canonical.
TraffSim3D-backend/tests/contract/snapshots/*.json text eol=lf

# `docs/openapi.json` is compared byte-for-byte by
# `scripts/export_openapi.py --check` (the CI gate that keeps the
# committed schema in step with the FastAPI app). The script always
# writes LF, so a CRLF checkout on Windows would make the check fail
# on a pristine clone even when nothing drifted. Pin it to LF, same
# reasoning as the contract goldens above.
docs/openapi.json text eol=lf

# The bundled demo-city extract (the offline Smart City scene). The
# backend's git checkout on Windows converts LF to CRLF (core.autocrlf),
# so the same file would carry different bytes on every machine. The
# parser reads XML and does not care about line endings, but a
# byte-identical asset keeps the repository honest: pin it to LF.
TraffSim3D-backend/geojson/福田中心(深圳).osm text eol=lf
